<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Ain Jalut</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1260">1260</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Ain Jalut · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongol-invasions-of-the-levant">Mongol invasions of the Levant</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Ain Jalut was fought in 1260 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palestine">Palestine</a> between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk-sultanate">Mamluk Sultanate</a> and a Mongol army of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluks</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qutuz">Qutuz</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baybars">Baybars</a> won, halting the Mongol advance into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>. It followed the Mongol destruction of the Ayyubid principalities in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> and confirmed the Mamluks as the dominant power in the region.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-ain-jalut.jpg" alt="Battle of Ain Jalut" width="317" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: MapMaster · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Campaign_of_the_Battle_of_Ain_Jalut_1260.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
